# SBL_COMANDO — Cursor / Agent Rules

You are working in the **SBL_COMANDO** monorepo (שולי בן לולו — ליגת כובשים יעדים).

## Hard path constraints (do not break CI/CD)

- **Production frontend lives in `base44-app/`** — folder name is legacy; **do not rename** without updating `backend/buildspec.yml` and docs.
- **Backend lives in `backend/`** — FastAPI + Alembic + EB `Dockerfile` + `buildspec.yml`.
- **Infrastructure lives in `terraform/`** — do not invent parallel infra folders.
- **CI triggers:** `.github/workflows/deploy-dev.yml` / `deploy-prod.yml` → CodePipeline. Do not change trigger contracts casually.
- Root `docker-compose.yml` is the local stack. Prefer it over nested compose files unless explicitly asked.
- `frontend/` is a **legacy stub only** — never put product features there.

## Where new code goes

| Work | Put it here |
|------|-------------|
| React pages | `base44-app/src/pages/` |
| Shared UI / domain components | `base44-app/src/components/` |
| API client / auth context / helpers | `base44-app/src/api/`, `base44-app/src/lib/` |
| Static brand assets | `base44-app/public/` |
| FastAPI routers | `backend/app/api/` or `backend/app/auth/` |
| ORM models / serializers | `backend/app/models.py`, `backend/app/serializers.py` |
| DB migrations | `backend/alembic/versions/` |
| Ops docs / architecture maps | `docs/` |
| Env templates | nearest package `.env.example` or root `.env.example` |

## Coding standards

- Prefer small, focused diffs. Do not drive-by refactor unrelated files.
- Match existing style (React + Vite JS, FastAPI Python).
- Handle errors with clear user-facing toasts (FE) and HTTPException/logging (BE).
- Uploads / avatars / rewards: durable storage via `/api/media/{id}` (Postgres `media_assets`) — do not rely on EB local disk alone.
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials). Respect existing env var names used by EB/Terraform.
- Do not scatter loose config files in the repo root — use the module that owns them.
- Keep Hebrew RTL UX intact (`dir="rtl"`, existing copy patterns).

## Brand / tab icon

- Browser tab icon and PWA icons must use the SBL logo assets under `base44-app/public/` (`logo.png`, `favicon-*.png`, `apple-touch-icon.png`) — not the old text-only "SBL" SVG badge as the primary favicon.
